  {
   "n": 9,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>\n\tLet (<em>G</em>, *) be a group such that Ο(<em>G</em>) = 8. Where Ο(<em>G</em>) denotes the order of the group. Which of the following is true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>\n\tThere exist no element a in <em>G</em> whose order is 6.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>\n\tThere exist an element a in <em>G</em> whose order is 4.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\tThere exist more than one element in <em>G</em> whose order is 1.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "None of these"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, B, C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(a)<br />\n\tLet G be a finite group of order k then every element of <em>G</em> will have order <em>m</em> such that k and <em>m</em> = 0<br />\n\t(a) True<br />\n\t8 mod 6 = 2<br />\n\t(b) False<br />\n\t8 mod 4 = 0 but it not necessary that there must exist an element with order 4.<br />\n\t(c) False<br />\n\tThere must exist only 1 identity element in a group.</p>"
  },
